{"name":"Pipe","hex":"#857165","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Pipe","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","An unincorporated community in Fond du Lac County, Wisconsin, United States. Named after the calumet (pipe) smoked by native Americans."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Pipe"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pipe (fluid conveyance)","blocks":[{"text":"A pipe is a tubular section or hollow cylinder, usually but not necessarily of circular cross-section, used mainly to convey substances which can flow — liquids and gases (fluids), slurries, powders and masses of small solids. It can also be used for structural applications; a hollow pipe is far stiffer per unit weight than the solid members."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Series_of_tubes_on_top_of_Shibuya_Stream_-89062.jpeg/330px-Series_of_tubes_on_top_of_Shibuya_Stream_-89062.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pipe_(fluid_conveyance)","wikidata":"Q41551"},{"title":"Piping","blocks":[{"text":"Within industry, piping is a system of pipes used to convey fluids from one location to another. The engineering discipline of piping design studies the efficient transport of fluid."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Mechanical_room.jpg/330px-Mechanical_room.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Piping","wikidata":"Q3679502"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Paris_-_Palais_du_Louvre_-_PA00085992_-_1090.jpg/500px-Paris_-_Palais_du_Louvre_-_PA00085992_-_1090.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Paris_-_Palais_du_Louvre_-_PA00085992_-_1090.jpg/1280px-Paris_-_Palais_du_Louvre_-_PA00085992_-_1090.jpg?utm_source=e